From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Subject: build: install the CMake export once, not twice

CMakeLists.txt calls install(EXPORT ${PROJECT_NAME} ...) twice.  The second
call differs from the first only by not passing FILE, so it installs the same
export a second time under the default name qmqtt.cmake, alongside the
qmqttTargets.cmake the first call produces.

Nothing includes qmqtt.cmake: the generated qmqttConfig.cmake pulls in
qmqttTargets.cmake.  The result is two identical exports shipped under two
names, which rpmlint flags downstream as files-duplicate.

Drop the second call.

--- qmqtt-1.0.7.orig/CMakeLists.txt
+++ qmqtt-1.0.7/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -181,16 +181,6 @@
     OPTIONAL
 )
 
-# Generate a CMake file into the installation, to easily use the library
-install(
-    EXPORT      ${PROJECT_NAME}
-    DESTINATION "${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}/cmake/${PROJECT_NAME}"
-    COMPONENT   Devel
-    OPTIONAL
-)
-
-
-
 include( CMakePackageConfigHelpers )
 
 file( WRITE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/qmqttConfig.cmake.in"
